Cc: Neha Kapoor <neha_kapoor@redwood.ai>, Grace O'Connor <grace_oconnor@redwood.ai>, Marcus Lin <marcus_lin@redwood.ai>
Date: 2027-07-08T10:45:00-07:00
Subject: Re: EastUS3 maintenance advisory — staged restarts, KV-cache preservation & customer runbook

Hi Sam — quick answers and follow-up items: 

1) KV-preservation: Our goal is to preserve in-memory KV where possible. For encrypted RAM-resident caches, we will attempt an in-place warm restart using the kernel fast-path so most caches remain intact. However, we cannot guarantee 100% preservation for every tenant due to edge cases; the runbook includes a lightweight verification query you can run to detect a rebuild.

2) Batch duration SLA: Target per-batch restart window is 12-15 minutes. If early batches validate cleanly we will compress later batches, but we will not exceed the advertised global window. If you can nominate specific CIDR ranges or service tags, we can schedule a pre-migration route cut for those flows so you get a clean 20-minute window for critical streams. Please send the ranges by EOD tomorrow.

3) Reconnect snippet: Included inline below for quick patching by your engineers: 

--- begin snippet ---
// sample reconnect (Node.js)
async function reconnectWithJitter(connectFunc, retries = 5) {
  for (let i = 0; i < retries; i++) {
    try {
      return await connectFunc();
    } catch (e) {
      const backoff = Math.min(1000 * Math.pow(2, i), 30000) + Math.floor(Math.random() * 300);
      await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, backoff));
    }
  }
  throw new Error('reconnect failed');
}
--- end snippet ---

Attachments: eastus3-maintenance-runbook.pdf, kv-cache-checklist.csv

Action items:
- Sam: send CIDR/service tags for critical streams by 2027-07-09 23:59 UTC if you want the pre-migration routing cut.
- Neha/Marcus: confirm final batch size and whether we can shorten overall window to 5.5 hours if validation is clean.
- Grace: send the advisory tomorrow at 08:00 UTC with the inline snippet and runbook link.

Thanks — Jonas
--
Jonas Weber
Head of Production Reliability
Redwood Inference
